Charge this and use it to find the portals.

>  u - a blessed magic marker (0:19)

Use it up and then charge it.

>  a - a set of gray dragon scales

I know it doesn't fit the role-playing but considering your
problem, I'd enchant these with a blessed scroll and wear
it. Between the 9 points of AC recommended earlier and the
14 you could get here you could be looking at a 23 point
improvement from a life threatening -19 to a comfy -43.
There's a 20 point penalty to hit but +13 luck and +17 XL
and your skill at martial arts should cover that. You could
just wear the scales for a while without enchanting them to
see if it's really going to make you miss a lot.

>  b - an uncursed +0 pair of buckled boots named WATER WALKING

Won't help on water, ditch 'em if you need to reduce weight.

>  Comestibles
>  m - 8 C-rations

My rule of thumb is 8000 nutrition taken to the planes. A
C-ration is 300 nutrition where a K-ration is 400, a food
ration or a lembas wafer is 800. Now of the 8000 I rarely
use more than 2000, but I expect to finish the game in one
or two thousand turns after I leave the dungeons.  

c - an uncursed diluted potion of gain level

This would get a few more HP, doubled by the OoFate. I
really don't think XL 18 is bad. I've taken characters with
XL 22 and 23 through the planes without seeing an archon.

>  g - a cursed rusty ring of teleportation

I'd wear this through the dungeon to shortcut some of the
walking. I don't think you'll need conflict until you get to
the planes.

>  q - a blessed magic marker (0:0)

Charge it. You need charging for 2 /oDeath, the Orb of Fate,
and 2 MMs. You need about 5 ?oEA. That's around 115 charges
and that's about what you have. If you currently can
recognize a ?oCharging, write one with the (0:19) MM and
charge one of the MM. If not, wish for a couple of
b?oCharging, charge the empty MM and then you will be able
to write them safely.

